From 942c3e79723f6530cb97ad1796a4d606b8f11849 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NickLabs Orbis <orbis@nicklabs.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:05:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 12/13] CachyOS tweaks for PS4 (selected from Nobara's 6.15
 cachyos-base-all, "cachy" part)

Ported from the CachyOS kernel patch set as Nobara ships it for 6.15
(Nobara-Project/rpm-sources baseos/kernel/mainline/6.15/0001-cachyos-base-all.patch,
patch 4/6 "cachy", Signed-off-by: Peter Jung <admin@ptr1337.dev>), keeping only the
parts that apply to a Jaguar/Liverpool console:

- CONFIG_CACHY scheduler defaults (EEVDF base slice 0.35 ms, migration cost,
  CFS bandwidth slice, SCHED_NR_MIGRATE_BREAK), HZ 500/600/750 choices
- le9uo working-set protection (vm.workingset_protection, anon_min_ratio,
  clean_low_ratio, clean_min_ratio) - keeps the desktop/game working set under
  memory pressure on the 8 GiB shared pool
- memory defaults: compaction proactiveness 0, THP defrag kswapd-or-madvise,
  dirty background 5 %, writeback interval 10 s, watermark boost off,
  swap readahead off (page-cluster 0, good for zram), vmpressure medium 65
- ADIOS I/O scheduler (selectable; mq-deadline/BFQ/kyber remain)
- evdev: free clients with call_rcu instead of synchronize_rcu (input latency
  when controllers/clients close), LIFO exclusive accept wake-ups
- kernel.unprivileged_userns_clone sysctl (default allowed; Steam's
  pressure-vessel container needs user namespaces)
- optional -O3 (CC_OPTIMIZE_FOR_PERFORMANCE_O3; not selected by Orbis)

Left out as not applicable: Intel/Xe, amdgpu DC/SMU (Liverpool uses neither),
PCIe ACS override, intel-nvme-remap, v4l2loopback, vhba, distributed ThinLTO,
T2/ASUS/handheld drivers.

Status: applies to feeRnt 6.15.4 crashnt-4.7 + Orbis; not compiled by the author's
environment.
